    "updated_at": "2026-09-09T15:38:56Z",
    "body": "CI triage for build 87903: all five failing jobs (`amd-mi355-multimodal-processor`, `computer-cpu-multimodal-processor-shard-2/4`, `nvidia-h200-mig-18gb-multimodal-processor`, and the aggregate) fail on the same model, `CohereLabs/North-Micro-Vision-Instruct`, with\n\n```\nvllm/transformers_utils/config.py:544: in _patch_legacy_rope_type\n    if \"rope_type\" in rope_parameters and \"type\" in rope_parameters:\nE   TypeError: argument of type 'NoneType' is not iterable\n```\n\ni.e. `ModelConfig` construction for a model with NoPE layers (null `rope_parameters`), unrelated to this PR. That was fixed on `main` by #55949 (18615ad1ee), which landed after this branch was cut; main builds 87930 and 87934 pass these jobs. Rebased onto current `main` to pick up the fix — @vadiklyutiy could you kick CI again when you get a chance? Thanks for running it.",
